#: src-en/data/events_special_storage.xml.append:105
msgid ""
"data/events_special_storage.xml.append$//mod:findName[@name=\"STORAGE_CHECK_STATUS_MV\"]/mod-"
"append:choice/event/text"
msgstr ""
"CLASS: Acidic Destroyer\n"
"\t\t\tFACTION: Acidic Growth\n"
"\t\t\t\n"
"\t\t\tAcidic Growth, in its expansion campaign, quickly learnt that the universe is a dangerous place. While they had support from the Gathering in finances and resources, they did not provide combat-ready ships, insisting on keeping guard on their own. Obviously, this did not help with spreading Growth's territories. So, the Growth started to make more than just civilian ships, quickly becoming famous for its advanced weaponry. But, as the armaments improved, its ship-building couldn't quite keep up... That is, until the Gathering shared some of their engineers due to the rising threat of the Rebellion and Coalition. After the creation of Acidic Cruiser, the next project required enough power to wield as big of an arsenal as possible. Named Acidic Destroyer, the new ship came installed with up to 6 weapon slots, achieving the biggest firepower it could without artillery, which was often not adaptable enough. This came at a compromise: the shielding of the ship suffered to allow enough power to run the arsenal. Despite that, the Destroyer quickly became Coalition's nightmare. As they say, a good offense is the best defence."

